 "blurb": "The over-under shot from a camera half under water: a waterline crosses the frame with the world above it sharp and the world below it green, hazy and magnified. The water reacts to how the camera really moved. A pan throws it up one side and it sloshes back and forth until it settles, a tilt leaves it behind for a moment, and the faster it slops, the more the surface ripples. Water line sets where it rests.",
